Z||000002||drednot||04-07-2001||09:50 AM||||your frame looks tweeked.  could it be fixed?  YES!  would it cost more than buying another fiero?  yes.||||reg||9
Z||000003||Fformula88||04-07-2001||12:12 PM||||I am sure it could be fixed.  However, it will cost a lot of money to have the work done.  You will definately have to have the frame pulled back into shape.  Put in a claim on the Sunbird's insurance and see what you can get.  Oh, and do not take their first settlement offer.  They will come up some if you press them.  I recently was in an accident with my dads 87 SC.  Guy in the lane next to me spun out on the highway and went right in front of me.  The damage wasn't too bad... hood had a small crack, one of the headlights had its frame crack and the nose piece was roughed up.  Total estimate for repair was about $3000.  We got $2000 out of the other guys insurance.  Instead of having it repaired, he bought a new Fiero... an 85 SE V6 with 4 speed with only 69K miles for $1900.  Its also in mint condition... absolutely NO frame rust at all!  So you may be better served by looking around for a new Fiero.  But its definately your call!  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tweek||04-07-2001||12:25 PM||||Yeah, unfortunatly I was making a left turn onto a busy 4 lane street.. was quite obviously *my* fault. Although its happened before, trying to turn left, I cant see due to the guy in a van stopped blinking his lights for me to go... and Im like, well no one must be there.. and BAM.. Second time ive done that. <P>Pulling things apart it seems that the only frame damage is right where the door latch is.. Trying to take that damn door off is a PITA! anyways.. Im keeping my eyes open for a cheap fiero, there is one near me for sale for like $200 that advetises good body, blown motor, maybe I'll just swap motors. mine duke only has like 93K. I wonder if a shop will pull the frame out for me and I can do the rest of the work.. dunno. anyways thanks for the comfort. awful depressing you know..||||reg||1
