Z||000008||Jake_Dragon||04-07-2001||06:24 PM||||If this was my only driver I would go find another one, plus now I would have a parts car that I know everything about.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I recently hit a tree and although the first inspections looked good I am finding little things wrong and I was not going more than 10 mph when I hit. Don’t give up if you decide to try and fix it yourself, it will give you more time to bond with your car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Good luck. ||||reg||7
Z||000009||84Bill||04-07-2001||08:15 PM||||This happened to my 88 Coupe (bent the door & post and did a number on the knuckel)only on the passanger side . It can be fixed but it will take some time a day or two. If you want to know how I did the surgery that included a junker that was destroyed in the front ($100 from a local yard)and a sixer of beer for my welder friend, just fire me off an email and I'll give you the blow by blow on it. Oh and you will need a can or 2 of undercoating and a can of color paint that matches your car. <BR>||||reg||14
